  "summary": "The released 1.1.0 portable integrity lab includes per-APID continuity timelines: inspect provisional gaps and late recovery, follow ambiguity boundaries and retain every original parser decision in the downloaded evidence.",
  "rationale": "The safe Rust parser, independent Python reference and seeded fuzz checks remain unchanged. An extracted-app journey independently checks counters 50, 52, 51 and 53, a recovered provisional gap and unchanged late-or-reset review totals, then compares the real downloaded report with the API result. Coherent Cargo/Python/npm versions and runtime notices keep the new portable release aligned with its source.",
  "limitations": [
    "Restricted record-delimited educational CCSDS profile; no live radio/spacecraft integration, raw byte-stream resynchronization or payload authentication.",
    "Timeline segments are review boundaries, not proof of true sender sessions; provisional recovery does not establish permanent packet loss.",
    "Unsigned desktop portable folders, not system installers or clean-machine proof. Three-OS extracted-native checks drive an owned URL; default OS browser opening remains manual."
  ],
